title: `set -o errexit` is errexit, and removing it is removing errexit
origin: audit 2026-08-07 — `_errexit_on` parsed single-letter flag clusters,
origin2: so in `set -o errexit` the `-o` carries no `e` and the bare word was
origin3: skipped. The long form is what the Google shell style guide
origin4: recommends, so the spelling most likely to be in a careful project
origin5: was the one greenwash could neither see armed nor see removed.
